1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:02,880
(Previously) You're new here, at least you
should learn how things are done around here.

2
00:00:03,307 --> 00:00:05,747
Since when do you have to be a gangster
just to sit in class?

3
00:00:07,323 --> 00:00:09,402
A new bidder competed against us
and they got the contract.

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,327
Who's that?

5
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:11,391
It's Monchaitrakul.

6
00:00:11,467 --> 00:00:13,107
Why are you talking to me?
What do you want?

7
00:00:13,131 --> 00:00:15,720
I saw you working alone,
so I came over to keep you company.

8
00:00:15,952 --> 00:00:17,240
I don't want your company.

9
00:00:18,043 --> 00:00:20,159
Can I ask you something?
Can we be friends now?

10
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,280
Actually, you don't have
to give me your shirt.

11
00:00:22,398 --> 00:00:24,160
How can you wear it
when it's covered in my puke?

12
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,200
[Sinittha Kongpurim]

13
00:00:26,344 --> 00:00:28,920
Anyone who has anything to do
with the Monchaitrakul family

14
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,200
- is not allowed to set foot in Kongpurim house.
- [Monchaitrakul]

15
00:00:41,811 --> 00:00:42,812
Hey.

16
00:00:44,824 --> 00:00:46,480
What's with the rush?

17
00:00:52,662 --> 00:00:54,520
We haven't hugged today.

18
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,161
I'm a little tired.

19
00:01:14,272 --> 00:01:15,360
See you in the morning.

20
00:01:25,208 --> 00:01:26,209
Tokyo,

21
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:29,751
we need to talk.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,500
"Juliet &amp; Juliet"
(Episode 2)

23
00:01:41,551 --> 00:01:42,552
Have a seat.

24
00:01:46,718 --> 00:01:47,719
What's the matter?

25
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:58,410
Remember the daughter of that chicken
rice vendor at the end of the market?

26
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:08,040
I went on a date with her the other day.

27
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,696
I booked a whole pool villa
and paid for her and all her friends.

28
00:02:13,726 --> 00:02:16,280
Now she won't reply to my texts
or answer my calls.

29
00:02:16,424 --> 00:02:17,864
She might've even blocked my number.

30
00:02:19,886 --> 00:02:21,960
It seriously feels like she ghosted me.

31
00:02:22,264 --> 00:02:23,800
Or was she just freeloading off me?

32
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:26,550
No wonder she ghosted you.

33
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,016
Just look at you. You're so cringe.

34
00:02:30,144 --> 00:02:32,245
Me? I'm cringe?

35
00:02:34,546 --> 00:02:35,930
Is that all you want to tell me?

36
00:02:36,567 --> 00:02:38,840
Hey, not so fast.

37
00:02:43,176 --> 00:02:45,760
I spilled my secret,

38
00:02:47,192 --> 00:02:48,193
now it's your turn.

39
00:02:51,193 --> 00:02:52,360
You have to spill yours.

40
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:56,640
That's our rule, remember?

41
00:02:57,206 --> 00:02:58,800
Secret for secret.

42
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,221
There's nothing to tell.

43
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,600
Come on, something's clearly wrong.

44
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,001
I saw you having a serious talk with Dad.

45
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,160
Has someone been picking on you at school?

46
00:03:14,822 --> 00:03:15,823
No.

47
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:17,641
Are you sure?

48
00:03:22,064 --> 00:03:24,344
Or have you been doing something
behind Dad's back again?

49
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,840
Actually…

50
00:03:36,559 --> 00:03:38,600
I may have snuck into
a bar using your name.

51
00:03:40,170 --> 00:03:41,171
I knew it!

52
00:03:42,766 --> 00:03:45,040
And I almost got busted by the cops.

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,960
That's it? Why are you so stressed?

54
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:51,650
Next time, just tell me.

55
00:03:52,704 --> 00:03:54,600
It'll be our little
secret. I won't tell Dad.

56
00:04:10,894 --> 00:04:11,895
I feel better now.

57
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,200
[Phakjira Monchaitrakul]

58
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,540
Are you coming to bed yet?
The teacher is about to lock the doors.

59
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,040
[Sinittha Kongpurim]

60
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:43,071
Yi.

61
00:05:43,472 --> 00:05:44,735
- Can I ask you something?
- Yeah.

62
00:05:44,759 --> 00:05:47,479
What did you mean when you said
our family's old enemy had returned?

63
00:05:48,374 --> 00:05:51,160
We're just stepping on each other's toes
in business, nothing serious.

64
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:52,185
Oh, yeah?

65
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:57,851
Those Monchaitrakuls
are nothing but merchants

66
00:05:58,118 --> 00:05:59,480
who exploit ordinary people.

67
00:05:59,846 --> 00:06:01,418
But when they realized
they couldn't beat our family,

68
00:06:01,442 --> 00:06:04,282
they all ran back to the provinces
with their tails between their legs.

69
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,461
Is that it?

70
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,280
"Tails between their legs"?
Are you just making things up now?

71
00:06:11,515 --> 00:06:12,883
You're still a kid, so stay out of it.

72
00:06:12,907 --> 00:06:15,587
As long as we're around,
you don't need to worry about any of this.

73
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:17,481
Push harder.

74
00:06:20,435 --> 00:06:21,600
Why can't I know?

75
00:06:22,744 --> 00:06:24,200
I'm a Kongpurim too, aren't I?

76
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,000
[We're Hiring! Many Openings Available.]

77
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,800
[Join Monchai Construction]

78
00:07:02,850 --> 00:07:03,890
[6-Month Bonus Guaranteed]

79
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,201
Whoa!

80
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,800
Your boyfriend is coming all the way here?

81
00:07:15,123 --> 00:07:16,124
My ex.

82
00:07:17,267 --> 00:07:19,867
Ex-boyfriend or not, who cares?
He had the nerve to show up here.

83
00:07:20,219 --> 00:07:22,960
Go take care of it.
I'll be waiting in the cafeteria.

84
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,000
Tong, what are you doing here?

85
00:07:34,534 --> 00:07:37,520
I just want to give you this.

86
00:07:44,342 --> 00:07:47,000
You don't have to give it back.
You can just throw it away.

87
00:07:49,334 --> 00:07:50,654
It probably doesn't work anymore.

88
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:55,720
You blocked me on everything.

89
00:07:56,987 --> 00:08:00,240
I just wanted to make sure
you were doing okay at your new school.

90
00:08:01,254 --> 00:08:03,080
Is it as good there as
when you were with me?

91
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:06,180
Whether it's good or not
is none of your business.

92
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,481
You should go.

93
00:08:20,048 --> 00:08:21,049
Thanks

94
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:23,711
for giving it back to me.

95
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,104
Of course I had to return it.

96
00:08:28,371 --> 00:08:30,160
It was a gift from your dad, wasn't it?

97
00:08:59,448 --> 00:09:01,670
Here's your shirt back,

98
00:09:03,064 --> 00:09:04,680
freshly washed and softened.

99
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:14,351
Here is the sweet filling, like I promised.

100
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:21,831
Thanks.

101
00:09:30,379 --> 00:09:31,380
Hey,

102
00:09:32,022 --> 00:09:33,142
have you done your homework?

103
00:09:33,862 --> 00:09:34,863
Do you want to copy mine?

104
00:09:35,152 --> 00:09:36,360
- Sure.
- Here.

105
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:40,200
Do you want to have breakfast together?

106
00:09:40,448 --> 00:09:43,160
You'd better hurry, or
Paew will eat you alive.

107
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,760
I'm talking to you. Are you even listening?

108
00:10:10,219 --> 00:10:12,640
I saw you hanging around
in the library for ages yesterday.

109
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,240
I thought you two had made up.

110
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,560
You had a fight with your new friend?

111
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:22,200
I don't even know if
I can call her a friend.

112
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:49,250
They are definitely in cahoots.

113
00:10:51,895 --> 00:10:53,850
We can't let them
disrespect us like this, Dad.

114
00:10:54,414 --> 00:10:56,894
Why don't I take some men and deal
with them once and for all?

115
00:10:57,294 --> 00:10:59,854
Our best move is to strike
before they have a chance to prepare.

116
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:06,560
Why get your own hands dirty
when there's an easier way?

117
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:24,041
Have you heard? The
company building the new port

118
00:11:24,150 --> 00:11:25,950
is going to lay off all
the existing workers.

119
00:11:27,163 --> 00:11:29,123
Ing's husband will be
laid off, too. Do you know?

120
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,360
If Mr. Po's broke, who are we going to
borrow the money from?

121
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,921
I hate Monchaitrakul.
They started all of this.

122
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:36,801
Should I start?

123
00:11:38,536 --> 00:11:40,462
Go ahead. What are you waiting for?

124
00:11:43,278 --> 00:11:45,240
Hello, my fellow students.

125
00:11:45,699 --> 00:11:47,528
I'm Phakjira Monchaitrakul.

126
00:11:47,587 --> 00:11:49,427
- Today...
- Are you from Monchaitrakul family?

127
00:12:57,203 --> 00:12:58,523
What the hell is wrong with them?

128
00:12:59,258 --> 00:13:00,258
You didn't know?

129
00:13:05,833 --> 00:13:08,246
Look, Monchaitrakul won
the bid for the port project.

130
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:13,513
[Monchaitrakul Wins Project Contract]

131
00:13:15,275 --> 00:13:16,435
How the hell did that happen?

132
00:13:17,408 --> 00:13:18,480
Dad never said a word.

133
00:13:21,259 --> 00:13:23,019
Isn't your family the
one that's still here?

134
00:13:23,878 --> 00:13:24,998
They didn't know about this.

135
00:13:25,198 --> 00:13:27,598
No one in my branch of the family
uses that surname anymore.

136
00:13:27,907 --> 00:13:30,840
I switched to my mother's surname
years ago, after my father died.

137
00:13:31,656 --> 00:13:34,056
Yours is the only family still using
the Monchaitrakul name.

138
00:13:35,271 --> 00:13:36,768
How are things with your classmates?

139
00:13:37,272 --> 00:13:38,752
Tokyo's in your class too, isn't she?

140
00:13:40,976 --> 00:13:42,456
That's why she completely ignored me.

141
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:45,390
I think it was because of this.

142
00:13:46,419 --> 00:13:47,440
You're acting weird.

143
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:49,638
Even when Tong didn't
talk to you for a whole week,

144
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,163
you weren't this upset.

145
00:13:53,507 --> 00:13:56,507
Tokyo's just a new friend, so why are
you making such a big deal out of it?

146
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,440
Honestly, I thought you and
Tokyo didn't even get along.

147
00:14:01,635 --> 00:14:02,636
I don't know.

148
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:06,080
We're not that close.

149
00:14:11,736 --> 00:14:12,737
I don't care about her.

150
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:26,521
Well, what a surprise!
My daughter finally texted me back.

151
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,440
What's this about the port concession here?

152
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,961
[FUCK MONCHAITRAKUL]

153
00:15:00,143 --> 00:15:02,063
Lovely artwork on the new desk,
don't you think?

154
00:15:15,144 --> 00:15:16,645
[UGLY AND STUPID]

155
00:15:35,696 --> 00:15:36,697
Tokyo,

156
00:15:38,670 --> 00:15:39,771
I got you.

157
00:15:53,504 --> 00:15:55,305
Hey! What the fuck are you doing?

158
00:16:35,846 --> 00:16:39,000
So, who do you think's gonna win...

159
00:16:39,152 --> 00:16:40,632
the Monchaitrakuls or the Kongpurims?

160
00:16:42,256 --> 00:16:43,950
We'll find out who wins soon enough.

161
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,720
Let's keep it between us at school. Forget
the Monchaitrakuls and the Kongpurims.

162
00:17:18,950 --> 00:17:20,280
Where's my PE shirt?

163
00:17:23,438 --> 00:17:25,598
Whoa! This is harsh.

164
00:17:27,155 --> 00:17:28,600
Damn, these guys don't mess around.

165
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,650
I'm done taking this
shit. Tell me who did it

166
00:17:33,014 --> 00:17:34,160
so I know who to go after.

167
00:17:36,432 --> 00:17:37,952
You're still trying to act tough, huh?

168
00:17:38,603 --> 00:17:39,604
You're all alone.

169
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:42,270
- How are you supposed to take them on?
- You're not helping me?

170
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:46,000
Count me out. I need to graduate.

171
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:49,120
I don't want to spend a
third year in 12th grade.

172
00:17:49,550 --> 00:17:52,790
You should stay out of trouble too,
especially if you want that university quota.

173
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:02,160
Just wear your regular school uniform
for now. The teacher won't mind.

174
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:33,806
Wow. She's got quite an attitude.

175
00:18:55,662 --> 00:18:56,663
You did it, didn't you?

176
00:19:08,379 --> 00:19:09,400
Gather around.

177
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,960
Class 6/3, line up on this side.

178
00:19:13,595 --> 00:19:15,160
Class 6/8, form a separate line.

179
00:19:15,616 --> 00:19:16,920
Come on, hurry up.

180
00:19:21,022 --> 00:19:23,144
Phakjira? What?

181
00:19:37,224 --> 00:19:38,225
What's got into you?

182
00:19:39,112 --> 00:19:41,560
Can't you just behave like
the rest of your classmates?

183
00:19:42,142 --> 00:19:43,342
You're always causing trouble.

184
00:19:44,067 --> 00:19:47,080
Then could you ask the
others to behave normally too?

185
00:19:53,086 --> 00:19:55,526
If anyone has an issue,
we should talk about it face-to-face.

186
00:19:58,158 --> 00:19:59,280
Don't start.

187
00:20:00,144 --> 00:20:03,233
Is your whole family
determined to cause trouble?

188
00:20:03,787 --> 00:20:04,788
I see.

189
00:20:05,382 --> 00:20:06,616
You're one of them, too, right?

190
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:10,341
If you don't stop, I'll deduct points
from your conduct score.

191
00:21:12,030 --> 00:21:13,500
Anyone got a problem with Blue?

192
00:21:19,635 --> 00:21:22,182
Come on, let's split into two teams.

193
00:21:22,766 --> 00:21:24,980
Mix the two classes.

194
00:21:25,539 --> 00:21:27,339
Don't pair up with your
own classmates again.

195
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,001
Here.

196
00:22:18,598 --> 00:22:19,599
Here.

197
00:22:20,150 --> 00:22:21,870
That other vendor's snack wasn't very good.

198
00:22:22,334 --> 00:22:23,335
This one's much better.

199
00:22:36,650 --> 00:22:37,651
Yeah.

200
00:22:46,158 --> 00:22:47,880
I thought you'd never talk to me again.

201
00:22:52,670 --> 00:22:54,390
Thanks for sticking up for me in gym class.

202
00:22:56,232 --> 00:22:57,233
Sure.

203
00:22:58,686 --> 00:23:01,440
Honestly, I'm not quite sure
how to act around you either.

204
00:23:05,166 --> 00:23:06,167
Do the Kongpurims

205
00:23:07,182 --> 00:23:08,947
really hate the Monchaitrakuls that much?

206
00:23:16,539 --> 00:23:17,540
Yeah.

207
00:23:27,139 --> 00:23:28,140
Honestly,

208
00:23:30,900 --> 00:23:32,720
we shouldn't even be friends.

209
00:23:43,283 --> 00:23:44,284
Hey.

210
00:23:45,792 --> 00:23:47,493
What did you draw? Let me see.

211
00:23:51,974 --> 00:23:52,975
It's pretty.

212
00:23:54,848 --> 00:23:55,849
I want one, too.

213
00:25:06,595 --> 00:25:07,596
I should get going.

214
00:25:08,248 --> 00:25:09,249
Okay.

215
00:25:25,398 --> 00:25:27,120
I gotta go, see you tomorrow.

216
00:25:43,726 --> 00:25:47,326
[Everyone shitting on the Monchaitrakuls]

217
00:25:49,566 --> 00:25:51,726
People around here really
seem to love the Kongpurims.

218
00:25:52,894 --> 00:25:54,814
How have you managed
to live here all this time?

219
00:25:56,070 --> 00:25:58,071
My mom's family keeps to themselves.

220
00:25:58,680 --> 00:25:59,681
You, on the other hand,

221
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:02,480
just got here and you're already
causing trouble with everyone.

222
00:26:02,624 --> 00:26:04,281
Which side are you on, exactly?

223
00:26:05,940 --> 00:26:07,260
The winning side, of course.

224
00:26:16,552 --> 00:26:19,000
I only came because Mom asked me to.

225
00:26:19,912 --> 00:26:23,000
I don't get why Dad had to stir up trouble
on someone else's turf.

226
00:26:23,336 --> 00:26:26,480
Come on. Just think of it
as checking up on the family business.

227
00:26:27,880 --> 00:26:29,230
That's what rich kids do.

228
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:37,680
Get out! Get out! Get out!

229
00:26:38,016 --> 00:26:40,680
Get out! Get out! Get out!

230
00:26:41,715 --> 00:26:42,716
What is it?

231
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,600
Get out! Get out!

232
00:26:44,824 --> 00:26:46,250
Sir, you can park over there.

233
00:26:46,840 --> 00:26:49,480
- Get out! Get out! Get out!
- [We want jobs!]

234
00:26:50,120 --> 00:26:53,600
[Monchai Construction—greedy,
heartless bloodsuckers!]

235
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:58,040
- Get out! Get out! Get out!
- [Bad people! Selfish!]

236
00:26:58,472 --> 00:27:00,880
Get out! Get out! Get out!

237
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:02,201
Get out!

238
00:27:03,835 --> 00:27:04,836
Phu.

239
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,120
Everyone, please calm down.

240
00:27:26,336 --> 00:27:27,337
Here's what I'll do:

241
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:30,520
I'll pay everyone their
final month's salary,

242
00:27:32,091 --> 00:27:33,880
plus three months' severance pay.

243
00:27:34,646 --> 00:27:36,680
We don't want it. We want our jobs!

244
00:27:41,190 --> 00:27:43,960
We appreciate the money,
but we'd rather keep our jobs.

245
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:46,840
Exactly! We want to keep our jobs!

246
00:27:47,256 --> 00:27:48,362
We want to keep our jobs!

247
00:27:49,123 --> 00:27:50,360
We want to keep our jobs!

248
00:27:50,750 --> 00:27:51,950
We want to keep our jobs!

249
00:27:52,264 --> 00:27:53,358
Please calm down.

250
00:27:54,152 --> 00:27:57,160
All the workers are being laid off

251
00:27:57,539 --> 00:28:01,070
because the government's
contract with the Kongpurims

252
00:28:01,683 --> 00:28:02,684
has expired.

253
00:28:03,224 --> 00:28:04,830
Monchai Construction

254
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:08,441
will soon begin recruiting a new workforce,

255
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:11,720
and every qualified
applicant will be considered.

256
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:16,500
We have only one disqualifying condition:

257
00:28:17,662 --> 00:28:19,142
anyone affiliated with the Kongpurims

258
00:28:19,638 --> 00:28:22,200
will not be hired.

259
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:28,440
We can't apply then.

260
00:28:32,558 --> 00:28:33,840
How do you know?

261
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,440
How's your new school?

262
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:02,080
Have you settled in yet?

263
00:29:10,590 --> 00:29:11,591
And…

264
00:29:12,462 --> 00:29:13,540
How's the dorm?

265
00:29:15,107 --> 00:29:17,440
You don't have to act interested now, Dad.

266
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:20,400
You never asked me about anything before.

267
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:27,400
I want to know why you didn't tell me
you were moving here for the port project.

268
00:29:30,616 --> 00:29:31,617
Well…

269
00:29:32,190 --> 00:29:33,240
It's grown-up business.

270
00:29:35,347 --> 00:29:38,800
Dad, our business was
doing just fine where we were.

271
00:29:39,820 --> 00:29:41,480
We didn't have any problems, did we?

272
00:29:43,425 --> 00:29:46,265
So why did you have to come here
and pick a fight with the local mafia?

273
00:29:53,820 --> 00:29:57,640
You haven't been hanging around
with that Kongpurim kid, have you?

274
00:30:00,350 --> 00:30:02,040
She doesn't even have a friend, Uncle.

275
00:30:05,272 --> 00:30:07,360
She's hanging out with me all the time.

276
00:30:15,560 --> 00:30:18,419
We're not close. We're
just in the same class.

277
00:30:23,500 --> 00:30:25,780
Dad, should we have her
transferred to a different class?

278
00:30:25,950 --> 00:30:26,951
Are you insane?

279
00:30:27,896 --> 00:30:29,270
Why does she have to move?

280
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:31,920
You're right.

281
00:30:33,870 --> 00:30:36,179
Then why don't we get the principal to
expel that brat instead?

282
00:30:36,203 --> 00:30:38,011
Come on! Are you stupid or what?

283
00:30:40,600 --> 00:30:43,040
Why don't we get our little sister
to befriend their daughter

284
00:30:43,350 --> 00:30:44,560
and keep her close?

285
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:47,120
That'll make things easier for us.

286
00:30:48,214 --> 00:30:51,238
I just don't want our little sister
getting mixed up with the Monchaitrakuls.

287
00:30:51,262 --> 00:30:52,840
- But if it's the only way...
- Hey.

288
00:30:53,624 --> 00:30:55,125
What the hell are you guys planning?

289
00:30:55,918 --> 00:30:58,198
Maybe you should ask what
your little sister wants first.

290
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:00,641
What do you think, honey?

291
00:31:01,550 --> 00:31:04,141
What do you think of
the Monchaitrakul girl?

292
00:31:33,872 --> 00:31:36,240
[Singing off-key.]

293
00:31:49,134 --> 00:31:50,760
What is going on with you?

294
00:31:51,398 --> 00:31:53,600
You've looked miserable for days.

295
00:31:54,107 --> 00:31:55,400
Yeah, what's wrong?

296
00:31:55,750 --> 00:31:57,760
Are we going to the dorm movie night?

297
00:31:58,566 --> 00:32:00,488
Tell me now so I can book the tickets.

298
00:32:00,512 --> 00:32:01,920
Let's go. I want to go.

299
00:32:02,219 --> 00:32:04,880
But don't get seats too close
to the screen. It'll hurt my neck.

300
00:32:06,843 --> 00:32:09,044
Can you two not talk
about movie night right now?

301
00:32:10,134 --> 00:32:11,135
I'm seriously stressed.

302
00:32:12,219 --> 00:32:14,100
What do you have to be stressed about?

303
00:32:14,910 --> 00:32:17,576
You've got money, you're good-looking,

304
00:32:18,040 --> 00:32:19,200
and your family supports you.

305
00:32:21,528 --> 00:32:23,760
I'm stressed because there's
something I want to do,

306
00:32:23,800 --> 00:32:25,440
but I know my family would never approve.

307
00:32:25,940 --> 00:32:27,500
I don't know what to do.

308
00:32:29,230 --> 00:32:30,231
Well,

309
00:32:31,683 --> 00:32:35,120
then don't do it.

310
00:32:35,491 --> 00:32:37,392
You'll always put your
family first anyway, right?

311
00:32:37,416 --> 00:32:40,176
Just do whatever your dad
and older brother tell you. Problem solved.

312
00:32:41,187 --> 00:32:43,987
She's stressed because she doesn't
want to do what her family expects.

313
00:32:44,168 --> 00:32:47,328
If she keeps giving in to them, she'll
feel like this for the rest of her life.

314
00:32:47,659 --> 00:32:49,760
Then just…

315
00:32:50,219 --> 00:32:52,379
do it without letting them find out.
It's that simple.

316
00:32:52,459 --> 00:32:54,040
Why are you encouraging her to do that?

317
00:32:54,060 --> 00:32:56,700
If she gets in trouble with her family,
are you going to help her?

318
00:32:56,774 --> 00:32:59,160
Oh, do you have a better idea than this?

319
00:33:01,283 --> 00:33:02,284
I don't.

320
00:33:04,014 --> 00:33:05,015
See?

321
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:56,980
[You kept me waiting forever.
I missed you, you know.]

322
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,500
[I missed you too, so I
came rushing back to you.]

323
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:00,400
[Then let's get some
food ready and celebrate.]

324
00:34:51,043 --> 00:34:52,360
Blue, you're just lonely.

325
00:36:23,544 --> 00:36:25,545
[Literature Exhibition: Romeo and Juliet]

326
00:37:11,030 --> 00:37:12,400
♪ To you ♪

327
00:37:14,549 --> 00:37:16,640
♪ The one who means everything to me ♪

328
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:20,120
I heard your dad's such a big shot?

329
00:37:21,560 --> 00:37:24,261
Don't forget, he's not
the one sitting in class.

330
00:37:24,650 --> 00:37:27,600
♪ Our dream seemed within reach ♪

331
00:37:28,398 --> 00:37:29,880
♪ But you ♪

332
00:37:32,040 --> 00:37:35,800
- ♪ slowly faded away and changed ♪
- I asked you...

333
00:37:36,315 --> 00:37:37,316
what's the filling?

334
00:37:39,147 --> 00:37:40,760
Good... feelings.

335
00:37:46,536 --> 00:37:47,800
Fine. Good feelings it is.

336
00:37:50,536 --> 00:37:52,400
♪ I'll be waiting ♪

337
00:37:52,979 --> 00:37:55,600
♪ Though it may be only a dream ♪

338
00:37:56,272 --> 00:38:00,640
♪ Of a better day ♪

339
00:38:01,451 --> 00:38:04,240
♪ When you return to me ♪

340
00:38:04,760 --> 00:38:08,720
♪ There'll be love and everything we need ♪

341
00:38:09,099 --> 00:38:13,040
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

342
00:38:13,488 --> 00:38:16,000
♪ You're the one who made my love... ♪

343
00:38:18,940 --> 00:38:20,720
♪ become real ♪

344
00:38:24,451 --> 00:38:26,547
Do we really need to make
such a big deal out of this?

345
00:38:26,571 --> 00:38:27,760
It's only movie night.

346
00:38:28,308 --> 00:38:31,755
Damn right I'm serious.

347
00:38:31,872 --> 00:38:33,632
We dorm kids only get
to go out on weekends.

348
00:38:33,957 --> 00:38:36,400
Stop sitting around and
help me pick out an outfit.

349
00:38:40,390 --> 00:38:42,300
- Ugh!
- You think it's cute?

350
00:38:44,683 --> 00:38:46,620
Which one do you
think? I think it's this one.

351
00:38:47,083 --> 00:38:48,360
- Yeah.
- Right? I think so.

352
00:38:48,600 --> 00:38:49,640
The color suits me better.

353
00:38:50,859 --> 00:38:51,860
Phakjira,

354
00:38:52,190 --> 00:38:54,392
you can't join the movie night tonight.

355
00:38:54,798 --> 00:38:56,400
You will be in detention.

356
00:38:56,960 --> 00:38:59,080
Your PE teacher told me

357
00:38:59,141 --> 00:39:01,221
you're still on probation
for what you did in class.

358
00:39:02,046 --> 00:39:04,920
What do you mean?
She said she'd let it slide.

359
00:39:05,256 --> 00:39:08,606
If she has to serve detention,
can it at least be on another day?

360
00:39:09,736 --> 00:39:12,960
Phakjira, you are forbidden
from attending movie night tonight.

361
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:15,606
As punishment for wearing
inappropriate attire in PE class,

362
00:39:15,630 --> 00:39:17,000
you will be confined to the dorm.

363
00:39:17,160 --> 00:39:20,137
You must also write a reflection essay
and submit it to me tomorrow morning.

364
00:39:20,161 --> 00:39:21,480
No arguments.

365
00:40:09,824 --> 00:40:10,920
I like the lights.

366
00:40:12,100 --> 00:40:13,000
Tokyo.

367
00:40:13,086 --> 00:40:14,887
More people showed up than I thought.

368
00:40:37,022 --> 00:40:38,420
How long have you been here?

369
00:40:38,480 --> 00:40:39,481
For a while now.

370
00:40:41,096 --> 00:40:43,560
Blue can't join us.
Our PE teacher wouldn't let it slide,

371
00:40:44,030 --> 00:40:45,520
so she's in detention.

372
00:40:46,344 --> 00:40:47,345
Wait, are you serious?

373
00:40:47,550 --> 00:40:49,150
I'm dead serious.

374
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:51,040
I feel bad for her though.

375
00:40:51,109 --> 00:40:53,120
She's all alone in the detention room.

376
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,640
Forget it. Let's head over there instead.

377
00:40:57,574 --> 00:40:58,575
Is this good?

378
00:41:02,227 --> 00:41:03,228
Tokyo?

379
00:41:04,158 --> 00:41:05,159
Yeah?

380
00:41:05,811 --> 00:41:06,812
Where are you going?

381
00:41:07,560 --> 00:41:10,200
I need to use the bathroom.
I'll be right back.

382
00:41:11,160 --> 00:41:12,320
I'll catch up with you later.

383
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:59,001
[STAFF ONLY. NO UNAUTHORIZED ENTRY]

384
00:43:21,147 --> 00:43:22,148
How did you get here?

385
00:43:23,352 --> 00:43:25,363
I climbed the ladder.

386
00:43:26,973 --> 00:43:27,974
What?

387
00:43:31,198 --> 00:43:34,160
I need to talk to you.

388
00:43:35,656 --> 00:43:36,657
Right now?

389
00:43:37,619 --> 00:43:39,440
We'll see each other tomorrow.

390
00:43:41,246 --> 00:43:42,247
No!

391
00:43:42,664 --> 00:43:44,680
I need to talk to you now.

392
00:43:45,802 --> 00:43:49,200
Okay, hurry up and say it.

393
00:43:49,827 --> 00:43:51,347
This is very dangerous for both of us.

394
00:43:53,400 --> 00:43:54,401
Okay.

395
00:43:59,968 --> 00:44:01,240
I…

396
00:44:01,979 --> 00:44:03,560
I…

397
00:44:05,547 --> 00:44:07,320
I think…

398
00:44:11,320 --> 00:44:12,600
I think I li...

399
00:44:14,958 --> 00:44:15,959
What?

400
00:44:22,758 --> 00:44:25,275
Why don't you tell me tomorrow? Okay?

401
00:44:26,751 --> 00:44:27,752
I…

402
00:44:29,880 --> 00:44:31,408
I think I like you, Blue.

403
00:44:37,472 --> 00:44:38,473
Yeah.

404
00:44:40,907 --> 00:44:43,083
I'm not sure

405
00:44:43,398 --> 00:44:44,459
what to call this feeling.

406
00:44:45,355 --> 00:44:48,182
I don't know if it's a crush.

407
00:44:49,286 --> 00:44:51,040
All I know is that

408
00:44:52,798 --> 00:44:55,590
whenever I'm with you,

409
00:44:57,219 --> 00:44:58,339
my heart never stops racing.

410
00:44:58,910 --> 00:45:01,080
And I never want our time together

411
00:45:01,352 --> 00:45:02,353
to end.

412
00:45:07,483 --> 00:45:09,003
So… I think I've fallen for you, Blue.

413
00:45:16,286 --> 00:45:17,287
But…

414
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:23,701
if you don't feel the same way,

415
00:45:24,619 --> 00:45:25,620
that's okay.

416
00:45:27,968 --> 00:45:28,969
I just felt like...

417
00:45:32,256 --> 00:45:33,257
I…

418
00:45:34,064 --> 00:45:35,065
needed…

419
00:45:35,590 --> 00:45:38,411
to be honest with you about my feelings.

420
00:45:51,424 --> 00:45:52,425
Well,

421
00:45:53,595 --> 00:45:55,040
I should go.

422
00:45:57,664 --> 00:45:58,960
See you tomorrow.

423
00:46:02,299 --> 00:46:03,300
Bye.

424
00:46:46,950 --> 00:46:48,920
I'm a Kongpurim.

425
00:46:49,072 --> 00:46:51,192
There's no way I'd get
involved with a Monchaitrakul.

426
00:47:15,740 --> 00:47:16,741
No!

427
00:47:17,320 --> 00:47:19,600
I'm friends with a Kongpurim. So what, Dad?

428
00:47:20,136 --> 00:47:21,137
Blue!

429
00:47:22,776 --> 00:47:25,720
You said it was grown-up
business, didn't you?

430
00:47:26,787 --> 00:47:28,600
So whatever feud exists
between our families

431
00:47:28,620 --> 00:47:30,100
has nothing to do with a kid like me.

432
00:48:06,915 --> 00:48:09,179
(Next Episode)
If our families find out about us,

433
00:48:09,203 --> 00:48:11,087
there'll definitely be a civil war.

434
00:48:11,464 --> 00:48:13,680
Let's just keep it between us.

435
00:48:15,616 --> 00:48:16,617
Are you dating someone?

436
00:48:17,259 --> 00:48:19,763
Do you really think two people
from rival mafia families in this province

437
00:48:19,787 --> 00:48:21,227
could ever make a relationship work?

438
00:48:21,275 --> 00:48:22,440
You think it's gonna last?

439
00:48:23,240 --> 00:48:25,939
All our distributors have pulled out of
their transportation deals with us.

440
00:48:25,963 --> 00:48:27,883
You can't let them
disrespect us like this, Dad.

441
00:48:28,480 --> 00:48:31,520
Why don't you meet up with their daughter?
